# Personal knowledge base (InterviewTTS digital twin) - contains private data.
# Root-anchored on purpose. A bare `wiki/` matches any directory of that name at
# any depth, and it was silently swallowing docs/wiki/, which is 42 files of
# this project's own documentation that the README links to. If a personal
# vault ever sits at the root again, this still catches it.
/wiki/
# Local Pi runtime state
.atl/

# Local code index. 23 MB of SQLite generated by CodeGraph, specific to one
# machine's file layout, and the index re-derives itself on any other clone.
.codegraph/

# The pre-audit snapshot of this project, kept on disk only so the two can be
# compared side by side. It is itself a git checkout, so without this rule a
# `git add .` tries to commit a nested repository as a gitlink.
original/

# Obsidian's per-machine vault config for docs/wiki. The wiki content is part
# of this project and is committed; this config is not -- it records window
# sizes, pane layout and plugin state that belong to whoever has it open.
docs/.obsidian/
